        {
            "over": "4",
            "ball": "1",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "Jasprit Bumrah to Rachin Ravindra, no run, fullish on middle, angled in, Rachin Ravindra gets forward to flick to mid-on",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        },
        {
            "over": "",
            "ball": "",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "Conway's game has fallen off so much. When he started off, he was a run-machine. Lots of technical errors creeping up. He often gets squared up playing off the back foot and then there's is this tendency to go across the ball as we saw today in the dismissal. He has been inside-edging a lot and also outside-edging. If you see his dismissals in all formats, you can spot the errors that have contaminated his game.",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        },
        {
            "over": "3",
            "ball": "6",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "Anshul Kamboj to Nicholls, no run, short of length and rising outside off, 137kph and Henry Nicholls shuffles across and shoulders arms",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        },
        {
            "over": "3",
            "ball": "5",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "Anshul Kamboj to Rachin Ravindra, 1 run, full and angled in on off, Rachin Ravindra with a solid forward defence to the vacant cover-point area. Is off the mark",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        },
        {
            "over": "3",
            "ball": "4",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "India with a lot of chatter behind the stumps.",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        },
        {
            "over": "3",
            "ball": "4",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "Anshul Kamboj to Rachin Ravindra, no run, fullish outside off, angled in a tad, Rachin Ravindra gets forward and shoulders arms",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        },
        {
            "over": "3",
            "ball": "3",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "Anshul Kamboj to Rachin Ravindra, no run, 135kph, short of length outside off, rising, left alone",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        },
        {
            "over": "",
            "ball": "",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "<b>Rachin Ravindra, left handed bat, comes to the crease</b>",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        },
        {
            "over": "3",
            "ball": "2",
            "runs": 0,
            "type": "ball",
            "text": "Anshul Kamboj to Devon Conway, <b>out</b> Caught by Rishabh Pant!! This time no doubts at all. Anshul Kamboj punches the air as he roars. Devon Conway walks off gesturing to Henry Nicholls that it angled in and then seamed away. Full and angled in on off, hint of movement away, just the hint, Conway gets forward to drive and the bat is slightly angled, just slightly towards mid-wicket and the outside edge is found. Regulation take for Rishabh Pant. India have the openers inside 4 overs. The bottom-hand came off after the drive. <b>Devon Conway c Rishabh Pant b Anshul Kamboj 4(13)</b>",
            "batsman": "",
            "bowler": ""
        }
